@startuml
title Database Failover Flow (RTO < 30s)
actor "Patroni (HA Manager)" as Patroni
database "PostgreSQL (Primary)" as DB1
database "PostgreSQL (Replica)" as DB2
participant "PgBouncer (Connection Pooler)" as Pool
participant "Consul/Etcd (DCS)" as DCS
participant "Account Service" as AS

DB1 -> DB2: Streaming WAL Replication
Note over DB1, DB2: Normal Operation

DB1 !!-> DCS: Node Crash (Heartbeat loss)
Patroni -> DCS: Detects leader key expiration
Patroni -> DB2: Promote to Primary
DB2 --> Patroni: Promotion Successful
Patroni -> DCS: Update Leader Key to DB2 IP

DCS -> Pool: Configuration change trigger
Pool -> Pool: Reload configuration (point to DB2)
Pool -> DB1: Terminate existing connections (if any survive)

AS -> Pool: Execute Query
Pool -> DB2: Route to new Primary
DB2 --> Pool: Result
Pool --> AS: Success

Note over AS, DB2: Failover complete within 30 seconds. In-flight transactions retry safely due to OCC.
@enduml
